---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Layout title="About" description="Why PromptForge exists and how it stays 100% free forever.">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 py-12">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight">About <span class="grad-text">PromptForge</span></h1>
    <div class="prose-pf mt-6">

      <p>PromptForge is a public library of AI prompts, special commands, tools and
      workflows — plus the guides that teach you how to use them. It exists because most
      "prompt databases" are locked behind signups, newsletters, or paywalls. Ours isn't.</p>

      <h2>The promise: 100% free, forever</h2>
      <p>Every design decision follows one rule: <strong>zero recurring cost, zero credit card,
      zero paid service</strong>. Concretely:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Hosting</strong> — static site on GitHub Pages (or Cloudflare/Vercel/Netlify free tiers). No server bill.</li>
        <li><strong>Database</strong> — the git repo itself. Prompts are markdown files; votes are stored locally in your browser.</li>
        <li><strong>Auth</strong> — GitHub OAuth Device Flow. No paid auth provider.</li>
        <li><strong>LLM</strong> — free providers only: Pollinations (keyless), Google AI Studio, Groq, OpenRouter free models, or local WebLLM.</li>
        <li><strong>Payments</strong> — none. No Stripe, no subscription, no paywall, no ads.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <p>The site is fully static. Content lives in <code>/src/content/</code> as markdown with a
      Zod-validated schema. A GitHub Action validates every contribution and auto-tags new
      submissions. The Run feature calls free LLM APIs directly from your browser — your key
      (if any) never leaves your device.</p>

      <h2>Contribute</h2>
      <p>PromptForge is only as good as the community's prompts. Fork the repo, add a markdown
      file, and open a PR — CI does the rest. See the <a href={`${base}contribute`}>Contribute</a> page for the full flow.</p>

    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
